    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eafa5012_9895bc27",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/vts/functional/radio_hidl_hal_api.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-12T07:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we generally avoid NOT_SUPPORTED for all APIs as we want consistent behavior and want vendors to support all APIs. However that will change with the work Daniel is doing for optional stuff but I think there will be a formal way to do it. For this I would suggest removing NOT_SUPPORTED, and in case it is documented with the 1.6 API remove that as well.",
      "parentUuid": "069f77e0_a102ede1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 315,
        "startChar": 76,
        "endLine": 315,
        "endChar": 97
      },
      "revId": "4c8bba26d3a2a4daeb6d19d4ccd7dfc74a1dbe04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20702bca_658ccd3f",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/vts/functional/radio_hidl_hal_api.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-10T21:43:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Grace, can you comment on this? Will modem be able to query card state when SIM is powered off?\n\nAlso, Jordan, if you are assuming CardState::PRESENT you don\u0027t need cardStateForTest anyway.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4c8bba26d3a2a4daeb6d19d4ccd7dfc74a1dbe04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2aaef5a6_70ed92df",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/vts/functional/radio_hidl_hal_api.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 1138138
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-11T23:06:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would expect the Modem to be able to return the cardstate still, at least: CARDSTATE_PRESENT...but now I am wondering about the other info: num_apps, ICCID, EID etc. and how they should be reported... If the sim card is powered off, but still physically present, it might be better to have the modem change num_apps\u003d0....wdyt? we can still propagate the iccid/eid info, but maybe show num_apps\u003d0 so on one tries to use the subscription when it\u0027s powered-off....\n\nThe usage of this setSimPower API has always been in the context of a power cycle, but we haven\u0027t really planned out what happens if we leave it in this powered off state.",
      "parentUuid": "20702bca_658ccd3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4c8bba26d3a2a4daeb6d19d4ccd7dfc74a1dbe04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16cbc6cf_579b89c4",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/vts/functional/radio_hidl_hal_api.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-12T07:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The good thing is it won\u0027t trigger an unsolicited ICC_STATUS_CHANGED, nor do we expect a sim state query (from platform to modem) during this window in a general case. I don\u0027t think we need to enforce behavior around it. Do you think this num_apps \u003d 0 part needs to be documented/enforced? Btw if num_apps does become 0 that will trigger SIM_STATE changed broadcast for NOT_READY, which I think should be ok.",
      "parentUuid": "2aaef5a6_70ed92df",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4c8bba26d3a2a4daeb6d19d4ccd7dfc74a1dbe04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "adfd0b1b_87baa633",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/vts/functional/radio_hidl_hal_api.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 1138138
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-12T07:38:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm so I\u0027m just concerned about OEMs that do actually want to leave the SIM powered off, but then upper layer didn\u0027t get a SIM state change and still thinks the USIM/CSIM are in READY state and are trying to use it. In that case I think it\u0027s better to force a num_apps\u003d0 state with ICC_STATUS_CHANGED / NOT_READY broadcast when we power it off. But still have the other identifying info like ATR/EID/ICCID so we know what SIM is there. As far as documentation...we might want to enforce it, so we can prevent the SIM\u0027s use during this power-off state. I guess this change will then become very similar to what we see when we disable the pSIM through the , enableUiccApplications() HAL (i believe the num_apps also becomes 0), but in our case we want that additional step of the SIM power actually being turned off.",
      "parentUuid": "16cbc6cf_579b89c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4c8bba26d3a2a4daeb6d19d4ccd7dfc74a1dbe04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b13c4868_d69691ef",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/vts/functional/radio_hidl_hal_api.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-14T01:20:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But in that case are we saying that on power off there has to be a SIM_STATE_CHANGED, but now instead of ABSENT it should be PRESENT with num_apps 0? If yes the comment in hal needs to be updated for that. Or are you suggesting modem silently changing num_apps to 0 (for when it is queried) but otherwise not send the indication up to us? This latter option does not seem good to me.",
      "parentUuid": "adfd0b1b_87baa633",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4c8bba26d3a2a4daeb6d19d4ccd7dfc74a1dbe04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3281efc5_00d55b9e",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/vts/functional/radio_hidl_hal_api.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 1138138
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-14T14:37:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, saying the former (Modem should broadcast num_apps\u003d0 in order to trigger a SIM_STATE_CHANGED, otherwise others may try to access the SIM when it\u0027s in ABSENT state)",
      "parentUuid": "b13c4868_d69691ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4c8bba26d3a2a4daeb6d19d4ccd7dfc74a1dbe04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
